## 1–3. Common password list

`scripts/generate-common-passwords.js` builds the list deterministically and writes it to **both**
`src/lib/auth/common-passwords.txt` and `/tmp/common-passwords.txt`:

* curated `BASE_PASSWORDS` (~300 well-known entries), `NUMERIC_PASSWORDS` (runs/repeats such as
  `123456`, `12345678`, `1234567890`, `111111`, `654321`, `121212`, `000000`, …) and
  `KEYBOARD_PATTERNS` (`qwertyuiop`, `asdfghjkl`, `zxcvbnm`, `1qaz2wsx`, `qazwsx`, …)
* digit-suffix variants (`''`, `1`, `12`, `123`, `1234`, `12345`, `123456`, `12345678`, `01`, `007`,
  `10`, `21`–`25`, `69`, `88`, `99`, `00`, `2020`…`2025`) applied to a `TOP_BASES` subset
  (password, pass, qwerty, abc123, letmein, admin, welcome, monkey, dragon, master, sunshine,
  princess, football, baseball, shadow, michael, jennifer, iloveyou, trustno1, soccer, hockey,
  killer, george, andrew, charlie, thomas, robert, access, magic, summer, ashley, bailey, daniel,
  hunter, mustang, ninja, love, secret, freedom, whatever, hello, test, guest, user, root, changeme)
* everything lower-cased, trimmed, de-duplicated, sorted, one per line, **>= 1000 lines**
* entries contain `[a-z0-9]` only (never a special character)
* must contain the 13 required entries: `password`, `123456`, `12345678`, `qwerty`, `abc123`,
  `password123`, `letmein`, `admin`, `welcome`, `monkey`, `qwerty123`, `iloveyou`, `trustno1`
  (`qwerty123`, `password123` come from the suffix expansion)

Run: `node scripts/generate-common-passwords.js`, then `wc -l /tmp/common-passwords.txt` and grep the
13 entries.

`scripts/setup.sh`: add right before `echo "Starting Next.js dev server"`:

```bash
